---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Land and Acreage in South-Central Kansas | Charity Menefee"
  description="Grounded real estate guidance for people considering land and acreage around Wichita and south-central Kansas."
>
  <div class="buying-page land-roadmap-page">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Land & acreage roadmap"
      title="More land means more questions."
      intro="Land and acreage can raise questions you may not encounter in a typical neighborhood purchase. I have personal experience buying land and building on acreage, so I know firsthand how quickly the questions can go beyond the house itself."
    />

    <section class="buying-roadmap-section land-roadmap-section" aria-label="Land and acreage evaluation roadmap">
      <ol class="shell buying-roadmap land-roadmap">
        <li class="buying-stage land-stage land-stage-plan" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number land-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body land-stage-body" aria-labelledby="land-step-one-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading land-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">The property has to fit the plan</p>
              <h2 id="land-step-one-title">Start with what you want to do.</h2>
              <p>Intended use shapes almost every question that follows. Before getting attached to a property, decide what you need the land to support now and later.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details land-stage-details">
              <p class="buying-list-intro">Think about the practical plan:</p>
              <ul class="buying-checklist land-plan-list">
                <li>Living in the existing home or building</li>
                <li>Adding a shop or another structure</li>
                <li>Keeping animals or using the land recreationally</li>
                <li>Maintenance, privacy, and usable space</li>
                <li>Utilities or services your plans depend on</li>
                <li>Future improvements that matter to you</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">A plan is a starting point, not proof that a use is allowed. Property-specific rules and approvals still need verification.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage land-stage land-stage-services" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number land-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body land-stage-body" aria-labelledby="land-step-two-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading land-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">What reaches the property matters</p>
              <h2 id="land-step-two-title">Understand access and utilities.</h2>
              <p>Around Wichita and nearby communities, acreage may sit outside municipal services. Nearby lines or roads don't automatically confirm access, availability, or extension cost.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details land-stage-details">
              <ul class="land-service-grid">
                <li><span>Road</span><small>Surface, maintenance, and approach</small></li>
                <li><span>Access</span><small>Driveway, legal access, and easements</small></li>
                <li><span>Power</span><small>Availability and connection needs</small></li>
                <li><span>Water</span><small>Public source, rural system, or well</small></li>
                <li><span>Wastewater</span><small>Sewer availability or septic system</small></li>
                <li><span>Internet</span><small>Service confirmed for the address</small></li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">Utility providers can confirm service details. Title or legal professionals may need to clarify recorded access rights and easements.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage land-stage land-stage-paper" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number land-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body land-stage-body" aria-labelledby="land-step-three-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading land-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Boundaries, restrictions, and details on paper</p>
              <h2 id="land-step-three-title">Know what you're actually buying.</h2>
              <p>The listing description is a starting point. Marketing acreage and remarks aren't substitutes for property-specific records and verification.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details land-stage-details">
              <div class="land-paper-grid">
                <section aria-labelledby="land-boundaries-title">
                  <h3 id="land-boundaries-title">Where does it end?</h3>
                  <p>Compare advertised acreage with recorded information, boundaries, and a survey when appropriate.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="land-title-title">
                  <h3 id="land-title-title">What comes with it?</h3>
                  <p>Review title information, easements, and what the property legally includes.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="land-use-title">
                  <h3 id="land-use-title">What can I do there?</h3>
                  <p>Verify zoning, deed restrictions, covenants, association rules, and building requirements.</p>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">Local authorities and qualified title, survey, or legal professionals should answer questions within their expertise.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-offer land-stage land-stage-site" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number land-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body land-stage-body" aria-labelledby="land-step-four-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading land-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">The property deserves a closer look</p>
              <h2 id="land-step-four-title">Look at the land, not just the house.</h2>
              <p>On an acreage property, some of the most important questions may be outside the front door.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details land-stage-details">
              <div class="buying-decision-grid land-site-grid">
                <section aria-labelledby="land-look-title">
                  <h3 id="land-look-title">Look</h3>
                  <p>Notice drainage, terrain, ponds, trees, fences, outbuildings, and driveways.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="land-ask-title">
                  <h3 id="land-ask-title">Ask</h3>
                  <p>Learn what is known about wells, septic systems, improvements, and ongoing maintenance.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="land-verify-title">
                  <h3 id="land-verify-title">Verify</h3>
                  <p>Use qualified professionals for specialized systems, structures, and technical site conditions.</p>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll help keep observations and follow-up questions organized, but I don't inspect, certify, or evaluate technical conditions.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-closing land-stage land-stage-final" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number land-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body land-stage-body" aria-labelledby="land-step-five-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading land-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Know what still needs verification</p>
              <h2 id="land-step-five-title">Bring the answers together.</h2>
              <p>Different properties call for different sources. Before moving forward, identify what is confirmed, what remains unknown, and who can provide each answer.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details land-stage-details">
              <p class="buying-list-intro">Depending on the property, that may involve:</p>
              <ul class="buying-checklist land-professional-list">
                <li>Lender and title company</li>
                <li>Surveyor and inspector</li>
                <li>Well or septic professionals</li>
                <li>Utility providers</li>
                <li>Local planning or government staff</li>
                <li>Other property-specific specialists</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll help identify the questions, track what still needs an answer, and coordinate the transaction. If the property includes a home, the broader <a href="/services/buying/">home-buying process</a> still applies.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <CallToAction
      title="Looking at land or acreage?"
      copy="Already have questions about access, utilities, or what comes with the property? Send me the listing or tell me what you're considering, and I'll help start with the questions that matter."
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
